                                    <TEXT TI="TI_1676746760">VCU communication verification fault</TEXT>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1826033865">YES</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_786029952">1. Check whether the LV signal terminal connection is normal.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_2124421553">Network Relate Diagnostic Active
System power mode=on OR wake up</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1660869490">Continuous</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1451217794">10ms</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_566248183">Check Sum continuous verification error 2 times; Maximum difference value of Counter (MaxDeltaCounterInit) ≥ 9, 1 times continuously (a &lt; 10);Number of times of continuous repetition (RepeatedDate) of the Counter value 3 times; During normal communication between sending node and receiving node, Counter = 0x0F repeats 1 times continuously)</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1730141131">Check Sum is correct; Counter maximum difference (MaxDeltaCounterInit) &lt; 9; The Counter value is not repeated; During normal communication between sending node and receiving node, Counter = 0x0F does not appear</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1126449708">Record DTC</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_186490916">40</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_802023948">1. The message alivecounter check failed.
2. The meesage alivecounter algorithm is different between sender and receiver.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_1132611432">Record the fault, DCDC continues to run and OBC.DCFC stops immediately</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
